        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): cap user profile cache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an unbounded in-process **`userProfileCache`** in the LINE send path. Profile lookups are cached for 5 minutes but had no size cap, so gateways serving many distinct LINE users could grow memory without limit.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nExtracts `cacheLineUserProfile` and applies `pruneMapToMaxSize` after each write, capped at **1 024 entries** with LRU eviction.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nLong-lived LINE gateways get bounded profile-cache memory. Behavior is unchanged for the first 1 024 distinct cached users; oldest entries evict under sustained distinct-user traffic.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- `extensions/line/src/send.ts` — `userProfileCache` Map and cap constant wired through `cacheLineUserProfile`\r\n- Diff: production change in `send.ts`; regression in `send.test.ts`\r\n\r\n### Behavior proof\r\n\r\n#### 1) Call-site regression tests (real Vitest stdout)\r\n\r\n```text\r\n$ pnpm test extensions/line/src/send.test.ts --reporter=verbose\r\n\r\n ✓ LINE send helpers > caches profile results by default 0ms\r\n ✓ LINE send helpers > evicts oldest profile cache entries once the cache exceeds its cap 4ms\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\r\n   Duration  1.20s (transform 554ms, setup 132ms, import 3ms, tests 985ms, environment 0ms)\r\n\r\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 4.77s\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Proof gap:** No redacted live LINE Messaging API profile-fetch logs in this validation environment.\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/line-cap-user-profile-cache",
